import LegalPage from '@/layouts/LegalPage.astro';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Dinn Pharma Stock"
  eyebrow="Documentation"
  updatedAt="September 30, 2026"
  description="How to connect Dinn Pharma Stock to an AI assistant and what it can answer about stock availability in pharmacies."
  lang="en"
  showLanguageNotice={false}
>
  <section>
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>
      Dinn Pharma Stock is a read-only connector that lets pharmaceutical
      industry professionals ask an AI assistant about stock availability.
      It covers executive indicators, rupture trends, rankings by SKU or
      retail network, the most critical points of sale, store-level detail,
      and nearby product locations on interactive maps.
    </p>
    <p>
      Every answer states its scope and freshness and separates observed
      values from estimates. The connector never changes stock, records, or
      operational data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Requirements</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An active Dinn account at a company whose contract includes Dinn Stock.</li>
      <li>An AI assistant that supports remote MCP servers with OAuth sign-in.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Access always follows the signed-in account: the company, portfolio,
      and contracted features of that user. Nothing outside that scope is
      returned.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Connecting</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>
        Add a custom connector in your assistant with the server URL
        <code>https://api.dinn.ai/mcp</code>.
      </li>
      <li>When prompted, sign in with your Dinn credentials.</li>
      <li>
        On the consent screen, review what is requested and choose
        <strong>Authorize</strong>. The permission is read-only and can be
        revoked.
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you can ask</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Find a product:</strong> "Analyze Dorvalin 500 mg for me."</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Follow the trend:</strong> "Show the weekly rupture trend for
        the last 90 days in SP, across all networks."
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rank presentations or networks:</strong> "Which presentations
        of this product have the highest rupture?"
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Open critical stores:</strong> "List the critical points of
        sale in São Paulo and open the first one."
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Locate stock nearby:</strong> "Where can I find this product
        near Avenida Paulista, 1578, São Paulo?"
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      The assistant resolves the product first and asks whether you want one
      retail network or all of them before running an analysis.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Available tools</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><code>stock.list_products</code> — find products, presentations, SKUs, and EANs.</li>
      <li><code>stock.get_filter_options</code> — valid networks, states, cities, and bricks.</li>
      <li><code>stock.list_saved_views</code> — your own saved views.</li>
      <li><code>stock.get_overview</code> — executive view: points of sale, SKUs, approximate stock, out-of-stock share, criticality.</li>
      <li><code>stock.get_rupture_trend</code> — daily or weekly rupture over time.</li>
      <li><code>stock.get_ranking</code> — rupture ranking by SKU or retail network.</li>
      <li><code>stock.list_points_of_sale</code> — find and compare points of sale.</li>
      <li><code>stock.get_point_of_sale</code> — detail of one store and its SKU ranking.</li>
      <li><code>stock.find_product_locations</code> — nearby pharmacies with or without stock.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>All tools are read-only.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Data and limits</h2>
    <p>
      Figures are observed or estimated, and each answer says which. Cutoff
      dates are shown with the result. Store identifiers are opaque
      references returned by earlier answers; free-form identifiers are not
      accepted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Privacy, terms, and support</h2>
    <p>
      Read the <a href="/en/privacy-policy">privacy policy</a> and the
      <a href="/en/terms-of-use">terms of use</a>. For help, see
      <a href="/en/support">support</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
